#. engine/messages/conflicts.py (ticket 19b): two sheets with one number, m0-screens §5's Question title, verbatim for two.
msgid "engine.conflicts.same_number"
msgstr "{copies, plural, =2 {Two sheets are} other {# sheets are}} numbered {number}"

#. m0-screens §5 and 6.7: "S-14 and S-15 both draw the 5th floor slab, bottom layer". The plans' titles as drawn state the storey and what they draw (the subject's word is the view conventions', which the conflicts do not hold). 21c's Question title must word m0-screens §5's verbatim from `storey` and `subject` once display words exist; this message is the Conflict's evidence line until then. It counts the sheets the Question holds (`sheets`), not the plans: a sheet may hold two plans of one storey. It names only sheets the Question holds (`first`, `second`: once one is decided, the first two still undecided); with one left undecided, it names that one alone, like a sheet already decided.
msgid "engine.conflicts.same_storey"
msgstr "{sheets, plural, offset:2 =1 {{first_named, select, title {“{first}”} other {{first}}} draws} =2 {{first_named, select, title {“{first}”} other {{first}}} and {second_named, select, title {“{second}”} other {{second}}} both draw} one {{first_named, select, title {“{first}”} other {{first}}}, {second_named, select, title {“{second}”} other {{second}}} and # more sheet draw} other {{first_named, select, title {“{first}”} other {{first}}}, {second_named, select, title {“{second}”} other {{second}}} and # more sheets draw}} {titled, select, same {“{plan}”} differ {one storey, as “{plan}” and “{other}”} other {a plan of one storey}}{layer, select, top {, top layer} bottom {, bottom layer} other {}}{sheets, plural, =1 {, like a sheet already decided} other {}}"

#. One title on sheets that may draw the same thing (m0-screens §5): one title on consecutive numbers, or titles equal but for a member-mark range, are a continuation, and one title on runs that draw different storeys, marks or members is a series; neither is a Question. `sheets` counts the sheets the Question holds: one, once the others are decided.
msgid "engine.conflicts.same_title"
msgstr "{sheets, plural, =1 {One sheet is titled “{title}” like a sheet already decided, and nothing read tells them apart} =2 {Two sheets are titled “{title}”, and nothing read tells them apart} other {# sheets are titled “{title}”, and nothing read tells them all apart}}"
